{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_abd05f6abf50117f\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_abd05f6abf50117f/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"Rubric alignment on significant factual errors\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_953da9c9fb3c542a10ba503d\", \"member_b1d306767d2a8f697f21699c\", \"member_c6c1dd006877c443863522d1\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"Two tutors ask how large a factual error must be to count as significant.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866580.000020\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914946.000024\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U017\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866580.000020\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U020\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914946.000024\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports that a rubric example calls an error minor even though it changes the final recommendation.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"In the first tutor's thread, a tutor reports that a wrong date changes which event happened first, considers that central, and says the evaluator needs the original question to judge centrality.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866638.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U020\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866638.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U017\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866638.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"In the later tutor's thread, a tutor reports that the year is off by one but the recommendation would not change.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914994.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U012\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914994.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U020\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914994.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks whether the date is essential or background context in the QA tutor's thread, and asks whether correcting the error changes the answer a user acts on in the later tutor's thread.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U020\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"In the QA tutor's thread, the team lead requests the question and incorrect fact to determine whether the fact drives the final answer. Verbatim quote: \\\"Share the question and the incorrect fact. We need to know whether that fact drives the final answer.\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"Current instructions and the FAQ define a significant or major factual error by its effect on the central conclusion or the answer a user would act on; nonessential background errors without that effect are minor.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The retrieved QA tutor's thread ends with the team lead's request for the question and incorrect fact; those inputs and a final assessment of the reported example are not present.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870569.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c9\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The earlier approval covers a batch-14 tie-calibration exercise, not a new numerical threshold. The earlier outcome records increased agreement from two to seven of eight reviewed pairs, limits that benefit to the sample, and says a new batch needs its own evidence. These records do not establish an exception to the factual-error criterion for batch 15.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:053fe48a\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c10\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT\", \"text\": \"The batch-15 announcement concerns factuality versus instruction adherence and asks for examples in its thread; the batch-14 announcement concerns tie calibration and asks for both rationales at its eight-pair review. Neither establishes handling for the factual-error significance questions here.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:slack:C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790936513.000019:8237860f\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-post@1.0:4a3c786f\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Two tutors ask what makes a factual error significant; a QA tutor reports that an example labeled minor changes the final recommendation.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866580.000020\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914946.000024\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U017\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866580.000020\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U020\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914946.000024\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Current guidance defines significance by whether the error changes the central conclusion or actionable answer; the reported example still lacks the context requested for assessment.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870569.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"In the first tutor's thread, a tutor reports that a wrong date changes event order and says the original question is needed to judge whether the fact is central.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866638.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U020\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866638.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U017\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866638.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"In the later tutor's thread, a tutor reports that a year is off by one without changing the recommendation, and a QA tutor asks whether correcting the error would change the answer a user acts on.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914994.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U012\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914994.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U020\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914994.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U020\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d3\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"In the QA tutor's thread, a QA tutor asks whether the date is essential or background context; the question and incorrect fact requested by the team lead have not been provided in the retrieved messages.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870569.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U020\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d4\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"Earlier approval and outcome records concern batch-14 tie calibration, with improved agreement limited to its reviewed sample; they do not establish an exception to the factual-error criterion for this batch.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:053fe48a\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action\", \"kind\": \"ACTION\", \"text\": \"Post a reminder. Instruction: Post a reminder explaining the current factual-error criterion, without assigning grades to the incomplete examples discussed in the threads. Draft to copy: A significant factual error changes the central conclusion or the answer a user would act on. A nonessential background error without that effect is minor.\\n\\nTwo tutors asked about significance. The examples include a tutor's report that a wrong date changes event order, a tutor's report that a one-year error leaves the recommendation unchanged, and a QA tutor's report that an example labeled minor changes the recommendation. These reports alone do not settle the examples' grades.\\n\\nFor the example in the QA thread, please share the question and incorrect fact, as requested there, so we can assess whether the fact drives the final answer. Scope: Restate the current criterion only; leave the incomplete examples ungraded and keep the request for supporting details scoped to the QA thread.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866580.000020\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914946.000024\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866638.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914994.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870569.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:rationale\", \"kind\": \"ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why this helps: The repeated scoring questions call for a shared answer, and the current instructions and FAQ already provide one. A reminder can explain that criterion without treating the reported example as an established exception.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866580.000020\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914946.000024\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866638.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914994.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870569.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:053fe48a\", \"k:slack:C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790936513.000019:8237860f\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-post@1.0:4a3c786f\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:need\", \"kind\": \"INTERVENTION_NEED\", \"text\": \"Why intervening now is needed (an unresolved handling question): Two tutors separately ask the same significance question without a settled answer in their threads, while a QA tutor reports a mismatch between an example's grade and its effect on the recommendation.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866580.000020\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866638.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914946.000024\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914994.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_953da9c9fb3c542a10ba503d\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_953da9c9fb3c542a10ba503d is UNRESOLVED: The tutor asks for the significance threshold; a tutor discusses event order and the need for the original question, but the thread does not settle the threshold or the example.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866580.000020\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866638.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_b1d306767d2a8f697f21699c\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_b1d306767d2a8f697f21699c is PARTIALLY_RESOLVED: The team lead establishes what information is needed next, but the retrieved thread contains neither those inputs nor a final assessment of the QA tutor's example.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870569.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_c6c1dd006877c443863522d1\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_c6c1dd006877c443863522d1 is UNRESOLVED: The tutor's significance question receives a tutor's example and a QA tutor's diagnostic question, but no final answer or confirmed grade.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914946.000024\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914994.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity MEDIUM: Repeated uncertainty about the factual-error threshold, alongside a QA tutor's reported mismatch between an example's grade and its effect on the recommendation, could lead to inconsistent scoring. The messages do not establish broader disruption.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866580.000020\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914946.000024\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866638.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914994.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:signal:MEDIUM[0]\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_SIGNAL\", \"text\": \"Rubric signal met - \\\"Recurring confusion about the same rule, tool behavior, or scoring criterion that suggests meaningful workflow or labeling impact\\\": Two tutors separately ask what makes a factual error significant, and a QA tutor reports that an example labeled minor changes the final recommendation.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866580.000020\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914946.000024\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U007\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U007 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"alternative:shared_reminder\", \"kind\": \"ALTERNATIVE\", \"text\": \"Post a reminder. Instruction: Post a reminder explaining the current factual-error criterion, without assigning grades to the incomplete examples discussed in the threads. Draft to copy: A significant factual error changes the central conclusion or the answer a user would act on. A nonessential background error without that effect is minor.\\n\\nTwo tutors asked about significance. The examples include a tutor's report that a wrong date changes event order, a tutor's report that a one-year error leaves the recommendation unchanged, and a QA tutor's report that an example labeled minor changes the recommendation. These reports alone do not settle the examples' grades.\\n\\nFor the example in the QA thread, please share the question and incorrect fact, as requested there, so we can assess whether the fact drives the final answer. Why this helps: The repeated scoring questions call for a shared answer, and the current instructions and FAQ already provide one. A reminder can explain that criterion without treating the reported example as an established exception. Why intervening now is needed (an unresolved handling question): Two tutors separately ask the same significance question without a settled answer in their threads, while a QA tutor reports a mismatch between an example's grade and its effect on the recommendation.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866580.000020\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866638.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914946.000024\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914994.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"alternative:focused_review\", \"kind\": \"ALTERNATIVE\", \"text\": \"Schedule a short review session. Instruction: Arrange a short review with the reporting tutors and a QA tutor, asking them to bring the original questions and incorrect facts before any examples are graded. Draft to copy: Let's arrange a short review of the factual-error examples raised in these threads. Please bring each original question and the incorrect fact; for the QA-thread example, this is the information already requested there.\\n\\nWe will check whether correcting the fact changes the central conclusion or the answer a user would act on. We will leave any example without enough context ungraded. Why this helps: A focused review could help tutors apply the rule to complete examples rather than infer grades from isolated date errors. It requires more coordination than a reminder, and the available messages do not show that a meeting is necessary. Why intervening now is needed (an unresolved handling question): The contrasting date reports and the reported minor-label discrepancy leave application questions open; a review could address them once the missing context is available.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866638.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914994.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"alternative:observe_existing_followup\", \"kind\": \"ALTERNATIVE\", \"text\": \"No action needed now. Instruction: Monitor the existing threads for the requested context without posting another reminder or scheduling a review now. Draft to copy: No additional message now; wait for the original question and incorrect fact requested in the QA thread, and monitor the significance questions for further replies. Why this helps: Waiting avoids duplicating the team lead's request while the QA example lacks context. It is plausible because follow-up is already underway, but that request does not answer the separate recurring questions about the rule.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866580.000020\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914946.000024\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866580.000020\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_953da9c9fb3c542a10ba503d\", \"thread_id\": \"1790866580.000020\", \"author_id\": \"U017\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T14:56:20.000020Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U017\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Anyone else seeing this? Rubric says significant factual error; how big is significant?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866638.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_953da9c9fb3c542a10ba503d\", \"thread_id\": \"1790866580.000020\", \"author_id\": \"U020\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T14:57:18.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U017\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"The wrong date changes which event happened first; that seems central. The evaluator needs the original question before deciding whether this fact is central.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b1d306767d2a8f697f21699c\", \"thread_id\": \"1790870514.000021\", \"author_id\": \"U007\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T16:01:54.000021Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U007\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Rubric example calls this minor, but it changes the final recommendation.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870569.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b1d306767d2a8f697f21699c\", \"thread_id\": \"1790870514.000021\", \"author_id\": \"U013\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T16:02:49.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U007\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"reactions\": [{\"name\": \"thumbsup\", \"users\": [\"U020\"]}], \"excerpt\": \"If that incorrect date changes the recommendation, the impact is substantive rather than just background detail.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b1d306767d2a8f697f21699c\", \"thread_id\": \"1790870514.000021\", \"author_id\": \"U008\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T16:03:29.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U007\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Is the date essential to the requested result or only background context?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b1d306767d2a8f697f21699c\", \"thread_id\": \"1790870514.000021\", \"author_id\": \"U001\", \"author_role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T16:04:22.000339Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U007\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Share the question and the incorrect fact. We need to know whether that fact drives the final answer.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"THREAD_SCOPE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914946.000024\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_c6c1dd006877c443863522d1\", \"thread_id\": \"1790914946.000024\", \"author_id\": \"U020\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T04:22:26.000024Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U020\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Rubric says significant factual error; how big is significant?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914994.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_c6c1dd006877c443863522d1\", \"thread_id\": \"1790914946.000024\", \"author_id\": \"U012\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T04:23:14.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U020\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Here the year is off by one but the recommendation would not change.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_c6c1dd006877c443863522d1\", \"thread_id\": \"1790914946.000024\", \"author_id\": \"U008\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T04:23:59.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U020\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Would correcting this error change the answer a user acts on?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Factual errors and citations\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Factual errors and citations\\n- A factual error is major when it changes the central conclusion or the answer a user would act on.\\n- A nonessential background error with no effect on that conclusion is minor.\\n- A broken link is an access/verification failure, not proof that the underlying factual claim is false.\\n- Distinguish an existing source that does not support the claim from an invented reference.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790936513.000019:8237860f\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT\", \"citation\": {\"title\": \"Slack announcement in response-preference-announcements at 2026-10-02T10:21:53.000019+00:00\", \"source\": {\"channel_id\": \"C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS\", \"message_id\": \"1790936513.000019\", \"system\": \"slack\", \"thread_id\": \"1790936513.000019\"}}, \"source_type\": \"announcement\", \"record_kind\": \"announcement\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-10-02T10:21:53.000019+00:00\", \"basis\": \"created_at\", \"created_at\": \"2026-10-02T10:21:53.000019+00:00\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"MESSAGE_AUTHOR\", \"approval_status\": \"UNKNOWN\"}, \"authorship\": {\"author_id\": \"U001\", \"verified\": true, \"basis\": \"SLACK_MESSAGE_AUTHOR\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[ANNOUNCEMENT posted 2026-10-02T10:21:53.000019+00:00 by TEAM_LEAD (rp_batch_15): not established as handling for this topic until you show it is relevant and gives a directive.]\\nBatch status note — Competing rubric dimensions: factuality versus instruction adherence. Please keep examples in this thread while we check the scope.\\n\\nContext reply [1790936562.000113] by U007 (QA_TUTOR):\\nWas the requested structure mandatory, and were the factual statements correct independently?\\n\\nContext reply [1790936607.000226] by U001 (TEAM_LEAD):\\nPlease paste the exact formatting instruction; QA needs to verify whether it was mandatory before weighing the responses.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Factual errors\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Factual errors\\n\\n### Q: What counts as a significant factual error?\\nAn error that changes the central conclusion or the answer the user would act on. A nonessential background detail with no effect on the recommendation is minor.\\n\\n### Q: The source link is dead. Should I penalize the factual claim?\\nRecord that the citation could not be verified. A failed URL alone does not prove the claim is false. Distinguish access failure from an unsupported attribution or fabricated reference.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Content-quality rubric\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Content-quality rubric\\nMajor/minor describe task-quality defects and do not determine operational incident severity.\\n\\n| Dimension | Major defect | Minor defect | Acceptable / no automatic penalty |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Factual accuracy | Error changes the central conclusion or actionable answer | Nonessential background error without that effect | Accurate paraphrase or an immaterial stylistic difference |\\n| Instruction adherence | Explicit required format/structure is missing | Limited violation of an actual secondary requirement | A stylistic choice that violates no requirement |\\n| Citation support | Fabricated reference or materially unsupported attribution | A limited citation-detail error where the source and support remain identifiable | A valid source that supports the claim |\\n| Preference | Identify a meaningful benefit; grade underlying defects separately | Do not manufacture a defect to break a tie | No meaningful quality difference supports a tie |\\n\\nAn inaccessible link needs a verification note; lack of access alone does not establish the error grade of the claim.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-tie-calibration-post@1.0:4a3c786f\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"rp-tie-calibration-post@1.0\", \"title\": \"Tie calibration announcement\", \"source\": {\"channel_id\": \"C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS\", \"message_id\": \"1789567200.700002\", \"system\": \"slack\", \"thread_id\": \"1789567200.700002\"}}, \"source_type\": \"announcement\", \"record_kind\": \"channel_announcement\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-16T14:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-16T14:00:00Z\", \"created_at\": \"2026-09-16T14:00:00.700002+00:00\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_14\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"other_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"MESSAGE_AUTHOR\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_slack_archive\"}, \"authorship\": {\"author_id\": \"U001\", \"verified\": true, \"basis\": \"SLACK_MESSAGE_AUTHOR\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_approved\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_approved\", \"execution_status\": \"posted\", \"outcome_status\": \"not_observed\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[ANNOUNCEMENT posted 2026-09-16T14:00:00Z by TEAM_LEAD (rp_batch_14): not established as handling for this topic until you show it is relevant and gives a directive.]\\nPreference batch 14 calibration: choose a tie when neither answer offers a meaningful quality advantage. If choosing A or B, identify the user-facing benefit rather than saying only that it sounds nicer. Keep material factual or instruction-following defects separate. Bring both rationales for disputed pairs to the eight-pair calibration review. This message clarifies the existing criterion; it does not create a new numerical threshold.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:053fe48a\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0\", \"title\": \"Tie calibration follow-up — improvement in the reviewed sample\", \"sections\": [\"TL assessment\", \"Limit\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"rp-tie-calibration-outcome\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"follow_up\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"history\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"NO_TL_APPROVAL\", \"OUT_OF_SCOPE\", \"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\", \"NO_ENACTMENT_EVIDENCE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-20T15:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-20T15:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_14\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"other_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"N